    ],
    "moment": [
      {
        "kind": "quote",
        "text": "He deliberately renounced any competition with the camera of the photographer, and claimed the right to arrange the [different] parts of what he drew in the manner best calculated to convey a certain impression, while preserving the utmost exactness in the representation of detail in each part.",
        "lead": "On Le Petit Pont, whose towers of Notre-Dame Meryon drew higher than they stand:",
        "source": {
          "author": "Campbell Dodgson",
          "title": "The Etchings of Charles Meryon",
